('guba',NULL,'Baku','Baku','71',71,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Baku to Guba to Baku (Same Day) Guba and visiting the Guba Genocide    Memorial Complex.   The mass grave, discovered accidentally during the    excavations for construction purposes in the town of Guba    in 2007, was a clear evidence of the genocide of the Muslim    population of Guba, committed by Armenian armed forces    under Bolshevik name in May 1918. The area is wonderful    on the left side of river Qudiyal-chay. Here you can see the    part of history of our nation and relax with nature.   Visiting Qecresh Forest   Qechresh Forest, also known as Gachresh Forest, is one of the largest forests in Azerbaijan, located near the town of Quba. Renowned for its dense foliage and majestic landscape, it features a rich biodiversity and is a habitat for various plant species and wildlife. The forest''s high altitude and clean, fresh air make it a perfect spot for those looking for outdoor adventures or simply to relax .',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',71.0),
